title: "Seeing with Electrons (TEM-view): a physics-based transmission electron microscope simulator and digital twin"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: dos Reis
    given-names: Roberto
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6011-6078"
    affiliation: Northwestern University
repository-code: "https://github.com/Advanced-EM/TEM-view"
url: "https://advanced-em.github.io/TEM-view/"
abstract: >-
  Interactive exhibits that let anyone operate an electron microscope in a web browser: TEM-view, a
  physics-based simulator of transmission electron microscopy (TEM, STEM, 4D-STEM, diffraction,
  spectroscopy, holography and Lorentz modes) that also serves as a digital twin; Ruska 1933 and
  Scanning 1938–2002, historical instruments; and TEM-view Kids (Electron Explorer), a K-12 and museum
  version.
keywords:
  - transmission electron microscopy
  - electron microscopy simulation
  - digital twin
  - STEM
  - 4D-STEM
  - science education
  - museum exhibit
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-11-10"
